From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zoom the page, not the body, in a 1920x1080 window

The body's CSS zoom left window.innerWidth/innerHeight at 1920x1080 while
the applications' elements stay in 1280x720: the video window the native
player gets (element rect against the viewport) covered the top left
1280x720 only, and the full-screen checks of the video shim never matched.
QWebEngineView's zoom factor scales the viewport as well, so the page sees
1280x720 as on the boxes that stretch a 1280x720 window.
---
--- a/webview.cpp
+++ b/webview.cpp
@@ -198,8 +198,13 @@
 void WebView::loadFinished(bool ok)
 {
     if (ok) {
-        if (size().width() == 1920 && size().height() == 1080)
-            page()->runJavaScript(QString::fromLatin1("document.body.style.setProperty('zoom', '150%');"));
+        // applications are laid out for 1280x720: a window larger than that
+        // (eglfs_mali, not stretched to the display) zooms the page itself;
+        // CSS zoom on the body would leave the viewport at the window size,
+        // and the native video window, computed from element positions and
+        // the viewport, would come out in 1280x720 of 1920x1080
+        if (size().width() > 1280)
+            setZoomFactor(size().width() / 1280.0);
 
         page()->runJavaScript(QString::fromLatin1("document.body.style.setProperty('overflow', 'hidden');"));
 
